- F481, runbook: the flag section now turns the flag on with
  `gcloud run services update storytime-app --project primary-advantage --region asia-southeast1 --update-env-vars STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES=1`,
  holds the way back with
  `... --remove-env-vars STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES` and the same service, project, and region,
  keeps Daniel's go for the step, and explains that `--update-env-vars` keeps the rest of the
  service environment. The text holds no `--set-env-vars` anywhere. The "off by default" rule
  of the round 2 text stays, so the committed adversarial runbook case keeps passing.
- F472 and F482, focus target: the end region holds `role="region"`, keeps
  `aria-label="The end of the lesson"`, and shows the visible line "This is the last step of
  the day." (`lang="en"`), so the region is no longer an empty, role-less div.
- F482, scroll: the focus move calls `focus({ preventScroll: true })`.
- F483, first render: a `movedRef` records a "Next step" press, and the focus effect runs only
  when `last` is true and `movedRef.current` is true, so a one-step day moves no focus on
  first render.
- New test `phase4-runbook.test.ts`: the runbook names `--update-env-vars` with the flag and
  names the service, the project, and the region; it holds the removal command with the same
  three names; it keeps Daniel's go next to the command; and it holds no `--set-env-vars`
  anywhere, with a positive control that fails on a planted `--set-env-vars` line.
- New test `phase4-lesson-focus.test.tsx`: a walk through day 1 ends with
  `document.activeElement` on the region `role="region"`, name "The end of the lesson", with
  the visible line, and with a `focus({ preventScroll: true })` call on that region; a
  one-step day clone (parsed with `weekSchema`) shows the region on its first screen with
  `document.activeElement` still the body.

